                <pb facs="1121" n="1001" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg1001"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/610</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Benton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-17">November 17, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        30.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 527</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirmation of the Ambassador’s
                    telegraphic despatch No. 94 of November 13th (12 noon), I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith the copy of a Memorandum furnished the Embassy by Señor
                    Calderon, the Chief of the Commercial Section in the Ministry of State,
                    containing a list of what he terms Spain’s “trade grievances” against us, which,
                    in the opinion of his Government, must be attended to before we can realize the
                    advantages of the tariff reductions accorded France by the recent Franco-Spanish
                    Commercial Agreement. A translation of the Memorandum is also enclosed.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Webb Benton</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1080-a1.xml" xpointer="d1080-a1"/>
            </div>
